8. MECHANISM -- academic preparation channels the SES advantage
============================================================================================
Step 1: SES strongly predicts the academic characteristics
   ABILITY  ~ SES : r = +0.463, slope = +215.68, R2 = 0.214, p = 0.0e+00
   PCT      ~ SES : r = +0.304, slope = +10.48, R2 = 0.092, p = 4.6e-187
Step 2: the academic characteristics strongly predict BA completion (adjusted model)
   ABILITY    b = +0.00288 per ASVAB point; OR per +1 SD (345.8 pts) = 2.71 ; p = 4.12e-17
   PERCENTILE b = +0.02184 per percentile point; OR per +25 pts = 1.73 ; p = 1.60e-07
Step 3: race itself also drops to non-significance once ability/percentile are held constant
   BLACK p = 0.680, HISPANIC p = 0.294 (bivariate race effects were p < 0.003)
Step 4: attenuation accounting relative to the bivariate b = +0.4729
   + race only        b = +0.3524   change = -0.1205 log-odds
   + academic only    b = -0.2171   change = -0.6900 log-odds
   + race + academic  b = -0.2316   change = -0.7046 log-odds
   -> academic characteristics do nearly all the work; race adds a little further attenuation.
Countervariable check (the academic variables themselves do NOT reverse):
   ABILITY  +0.00374 -> +0.00267, still p = 4.42e-16
   PCT      +0.04502 -> +0.02184, still p = 1.28e-07

