9. LIMITATIONS AND CAVEATS
============================================================================================
 * "curriculum" appears in the dataset documentation but is absent from the delivered file,
   so the academic block is limited to ASVAB ability + class percentile (coverage limitation).
 * FAMILY SIZE is a family-resource/background variable, not an academic-record variable.
   Including it flips the adjusted SES coefficient POSITIVE (+0.2951 p=.0086 without sex;
   +0.2906 p=.0097 with sex). The answer is therefore CONDITIONAL on that boundary.
 * Adding sex does not change the conclusion (b = -0.2379, p = 0.018).
 * The published pair (0.3636 -> -0.2293) is matched qualitatively and closely, not to the
   decimal; expected given a different sample/estimator/α. No specification was tuned to it.
 * Rare outcome (2.69%), cross-sectional observational data, no sampling weights available.
 * The residual negative coefficient is suppression / over-adjustment, NOT evidence that
   higher SES harms degree attainment.

